course: dictionary
lesson: 1207
title: Buddhist: a person or a thing
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one job in a sentence. «Buddhist» can name a person, or it can describe something. Look at the words around it to see which job it does.
explain: «Many Buddhists do not believe in a creator God.» Here Buddhists are people, so the word is a noun. «Mei's Buddhist grandma believes in rebirth» uses Buddhist to describe grandma, so it is an adjective.
explain: Try swapping in the meaning. A Buddhist is a person who follows Buddhism. If «a person who follows Buddhism» fits the sentence, you have a noun. If the sentence needs «to do with Buddhism», you have an adjective, as in «a Buddhist temple».
fact: A Buddhist is a person who follows Buddhism.
fact: Buddhism is the religion based on the teachings of the Buddha, Siddhartha Gautama.
fact: «Buddha» means "awakened one", and Buddhists generally see him as a teacher, not as a god.
fact: Buddhists follow his teachings about ending suffering, through the Eightfold Path, meditation and kindness.
fact: Many Buddhists live in Asia, and also in the UK, USA, Canada and Australia.
exercise: In «Many Buddhists do not believe in a creator God», what kind of word is Buddhists? | An adverb, telling how | *A noun, naming people | A verb, showing an action | An adjective, describing a thing
exercise: In «a Buddhist temple», what does Buddhist tell you? | *That the temple is to do with Buddhism | That the temple is very tall | That the temple is empty | That the temple was built last year
exercise: «"Buddha" means "awakened one"». What does "awakened one" mean? | A person who has woken up to truth | A holy book | A monk who wears orange robes | *A teacher who is seen as a wise person
test: Mei's «Buddhist grandma believes in rebirth». What is a Buddhist? | A type of food eaten at festivals | *A person who follows Buddhism | A kind of building with a tower | A holy book printed in 868 AD
test: «Buddhist monks often wear orange or maroon robes.» What colours are these robes? | *Orange or maroon | Blue and white | Green and yellow | Black and grey
exam: Which sentence uses Buddhist as a noun? | «The Buddhist Udanavarga is an old text.» | «A Buddhist temple stands on the hill.» | «Buddhist monks often wear orange robes.» | *«Many Buddhists live in Asia.»
